  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ga music and dance of Accra built around the gome, a large wooden box-frame drum that the player sits on and re-pitches by pressing the head with his heels; it is traced to Ga workers returning from Fernando Po (Bioko). Call-and-response songs are accompanied by gome, bells, rattles and handclaps; generic cards stand in for the bell and rattle.",
